          %p
            In the monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝕏
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝕏
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{X}, \mathbb{X}]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell: T \Rightarrow T^2
            being a cosemigroup. The second diagram corresponds to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c: T^2 \Rightarrow T^2
            acting as a symmetry, and the third and fourth diagrams state that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
            is a symmetric cosemigroup.
          %ul
            %li
              Universality of the vertical lift: Define the map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mn 0
                        %mi T
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu := T(+) \circ \langle \ell \circ \pi_0, 0_T \circ \pi_1 \rangle
